Third-party software

The ned binary is built from this repository (MIT, see LICENSE) and the Go
modules listed in go.mod, each under its own open-source license.

The ned-minimal image released alongside ned contains:

- Debian trixie packages, including Chromium, Xvfb, x11vnc, JWM, xterm, and
  their dependencies. Each package's license is in the image at
  /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
- noVNC web files taken from Debian's novnc package (MPL-2.0; see
  /usr/share/doc/novnc/copyright in the image).
- Scripts from this repository (MIT).

The image does not contain Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Grok CLI, or
opencode. ned-agent-install downloads each one from its vendor when you choose
to sign in to it, under that vendor's own license and terms.
